WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.670 --> 00:00:05.500
Floods can carry hepatitis A and hepatitis E into drinking water and food.

2
00:00:05.630 --> 00:00:07.780
These viruses attack the liver.

3
00:00:07.870 --> 00:00:12.700
Most people get better, but hepatitis E can be very dangerous in pregnancy.

4
00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.700
Here is how to protect your family.

5
00:00:15.586 --> 00:00:19.336
Both viruses are passed in the faeces of infected people.

6
00:00:19.385 --> 00:00:24.186
When floodwater or overflowing latrines reach wells, tanks and food,

7
00:00:24.186 --> 00:00:25.696
the virus gets in.

8
00:00:25.866 --> 00:00:29.856
Dirty hands pass it on too, especially in crowded shelters.

9
00:00:30.742 --> 00:00:36.422
Signs can start weeks after the virus gets in: yellow eyes or skin, dark urine,

10
00:00:36.422 --> 00:00:41.291
pale stools, tiredness, feeling sick, and not wanting to eat.

11
00:00:41.582 --> 00:00:46.772
Young children often show no signs, but they can still pass the virus on.

12
00:00:46.932 --> 00:00:51.132
A pregnant woman with these signs must go to a health facility at once,

13
00:00:51.132 --> 00:00:54.282
because hepatitis E can kill in pregnancy.

14
00:00:55.162 --> 00:00:57.642
First, make drinking water safe.

15
00:00:57.642 --> 00:01:00.992
Bring the water to a rolling boil, with big bubbles,

16
00:01:01.082 --> 00:01:05.232
then let it cool with the lid on, and keep it in a clean, covered container.

17
00:01:05.241 --> 00:01:10.232
If you cannot boil it, use water treatment tablets exactly as the packet says.

18
00:01:11.110 --> 00:01:14.900
Second, wash your hands with soap and clean water.

19
00:01:15.150 --> 00:01:17.390
Wet your hands and rub in soap.

20
00:01:17.390 --> 00:01:22.860
Scrub every part: palms, backs, between the fingers and under the nails.

21
00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.339
Rinse, and let them dry in the air.

22
00:01:25.550 --> 00:01:29.270
Do it after the toilet, after cleaning a child, before cooking,

23
00:01:29.270 --> 00:01:31.780
and before eating or feeding a child.

24
00:01:32.674 --> 00:01:35.504
Third, keep faeces away from water.

25
00:01:35.593 --> 00:01:40.744
Always use a latrine, never open ground, and keep latrines far from wells.

26
00:01:40.874 --> 00:01:45.303
Put children's faeces in the latrine too, and wash your hands afterwards.

27
00:01:46.174 --> 00:01:48.413
Fourth, make food safe.

28
00:01:48.413 --> 00:01:51.164
Cook food well and eat it while it is hot.

29
00:01:51.334 --> 00:01:55.084
Wash fruit with safe water and peel it, and keep food covered.

30
00:01:55.978 --> 00:01:59.777
If someone has yellow eyes or skin, take them to a health worker.

31
00:01:59.777 --> 00:02:03.778
There is no special medicine: the body heals itself with rest,

32
00:02:03.778 --> 00:02:06.048
food and plenty of safe water.

33
00:02:06.057 --> 00:02:10.137
Do not give medicines or other remedies unless a health worker says so,

34
00:02:10.137 --> 00:02:11.808
because they can harm the liver.

35
00:02:11.888 --> 00:02:16.928
Go at once if the person is pregnant, very sleepy or confused, bleeding,

36
00:02:16.928 --> 00:02:18.718
or cannot stop vomiting.

37
00:02:19.582 --> 00:02:23.301
Where health workers offer the hepatitis A vaccine, take it.

38
00:02:23.301 --> 00:02:27.862
Safe water, clean hands, and for yellow eyes, a health worker.

39
00:02:27.862 --> 00:02:29.492
Share this with your family.
